All files under `src/doubao_input/doubao/` are derived from the Linux port of
doubao-murmur (`doubao-murmur/linux/`). Each file carries a docstring
attribution to the original Swift source file (e.g., "Mirrors
DoubaoASRClient.swift"). Modifications from the upstream code are:

  1. Internal package imports rewritten from `doubao_murmur.xxx` to
     `doubao_input.doubao.xxx`.
  2. Resource path lookups (`_load_js_resource`) rewritten to read from
     `../login/resources/` instead of `importlib.resources`.
  3. `audio_capture.py`: added an `on_rms` callback hook (int16 RMS
     computed in the audio thread) to drive a real-time waveform in the
     overlay. Upstream only sent raw PCM downstream.
  4. `transcription.py`: added `handle_press()` / `handle_release()`
     methods and a 150 ms debounce (`MIN_PRESS_DURATION`) on top of the
     upstream `handle_toggle()` API, converting the toggle interaction
     into a push-to-hold (push-to-talk) interaction.
  5. `login_window.py`: window title changed from "Doubao Murmur - 登录"
     to "登录豆包" (plus the app icon), so the upstream project name is not
     leaked into this app's UI.

Everything else under `src/doubao_input/` (trigger/, inject/, ui/, hud/,
app.py, __main__.py) is original work for this project.

Tests under `tests/probe/` are original work.

## Desktop user interface: Myna (Canonical Ltd.)

The desktop presentation layer is modelled on / wired to
**Myna** (https://github.com/canonical/myna), which is licensed under the
**GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 or later**:

  - The application icon (`src/doubao_input/resources/logo.svg`, installed
    as `debian/doubao-input.svg`) is Myna's icon
    (`client/data/icons/hicolor/scalable/apps/com.canonical.Myna.svg`),
    used unmodified.
  - The optional floating indicator is drawn by Myna's `myna-hud`
    renderer, driven over the `com.canonical.Myna.Dictation` D-Bus
    interface (`src/doubao_input/hud/`). No Myna source code is linked
    into or compiled with this project: the renderer is a separate
    process, built from Myna's own source tree by
    `scripts/build-myna-hud.sh`, and the GNOME Shell overlay host is
    installed from Myna's tree by `scripts/install-gnome-extension.sh`.
  - The settings window (`src/doubao_input/ui/control_window.py`) is
    original code written in Myna Settings' libadwaita style
    (Adw.ApplicationWindow / ToolbarView / ViewStack / PreferencesPage);
    it is a re-implementation of the look, not a copy of Myna's source.

Because Myna is AGPL-3.0-or-later and its icon is used as an asset here,
this notice records the attribution; the Myna-derived binaries are only
ever run as separate processes and are not distributed by this project.